  26:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  27:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  28:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  * \defgroup IfxLld_Egtm_Tom_Timer_Usage How to use the EGTM TOM Timer Driver
  29:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  * \ingroup IfxLld_Egtm_Tom_Timer
  30:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  31:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   This driver implements the timer functionalities.
  32:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  33:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  * \section specific Specific Implementation
  34:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   The timer functionality is implemented using either a single or 2 TOM channels. The decision t
  35:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   depending on the following requirements:
  36:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   - relative position of the timer channel to the other channels used if any
  37:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   - need to trigger another module, for example ADC triggering.
  38:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  39:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   Single TOM channel is used for the timer and trigger functionalities.
  40:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   The internal trigger signal is generated when the counter CN0 reach the CM0 compare register. 
  41:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   trigger is used to reset the CN0 counter and simultaneously transfer the shadow values for the
  42:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   and trigger edge (SR1->CM1). The internal trigger is used as a trigger input to the next TOM c
  43:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   The trigger signal (output trigger) is generated by the CM0 and CM1 compare values. Depending 
  44:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   edge \ref IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer_Config "configuration", the CM0 will reset, and the CM1 will set t
  45:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  46:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   In case 2 TOM channels are used for the timer and trigger functionalities,
  47:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   the 1st channel (CHz) is used for the generation of the period,  and the 2nd channel (CHz+n) i
  48:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  49:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   The CHz TOM channel generates the internal trigger signal when the counter CN0 reach the CM0 c
  50:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   The value of CM0 of CHz act as the period value. This internal trigger is used to reset the  C
  51:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   transfer the shadow period value (SR0->CM0). The internal trigger is used as an input for the 
  52:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  53:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   The CHz+n TOM channel, uses the internal trigger signal to simultaneously resets the
  54:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   counter CN0, and transfer the shadow values used for the generation of the trigger falling and
  55:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   The internal trigger is used as a trigger input to the next TOM channel.
  56:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   Depending on the trigger signal active edge \ref IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer_Config "configuration", the
  57:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   In orter to have a similar behaviour to the single channel implementation,
  58:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   the CM0 is set to the same value as CHz CM0, and CM1 is used for the trigger edge.
  59:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  60:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   In order to ensure a coherent update of all registers, the internal trigger must be disable be
  61:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   the timer and trigger shadow values, and enabled once the update is done. The transfer will oc
  62:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  63:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   - Resources used:
  64:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *       - if the trigger channel is identical to the timer channel, only one TOM channels is used.
  65:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *       - if the trigger channel is different from the timer channel, 2 TOM channels are used.
  66:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *       - All channels used must be of the same TOM and TOM TGC.
  67:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   - The timer counting direction is limited to \ref IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer_CountDir_up.
  68:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   - If the TOM trigger channel is not the same as the TOM timer channels.
  69:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *       - The TOM channel used for the trigger must have a lower index than the TOM channels.
  70:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *         used for the timer.
  71:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *       - the TOM channels must be contiguous, unless specified by the driver using the timer driv
  72:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  73:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *  Note: the timer and trigger must be part of the same TGC, but PWM channels can be of different 
  74:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  75:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *   For a detailed configuration of the microcontroller, see \ref IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer_init().
  76:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
  77:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Tom/Timer/IfxEgtm_Tom_Timer.h ****  *
